Z||000000||Spyder||05-23-2000||12:26 PM||||How about a VOTE To Delete Option?:<P>This would be when someone gets out of hand, the members can vote to have a thread or post deleted after X amount of people pushed the delete option.<P>Remember when those kids got on here and did all the cussing and name calling. (the reason we have IP logging)<BR>We could have ran them off in the first few minuets. <BR>Also It would be more self governing where Cliff wouldn’t  have to break out the mop and broom to clean up the messes.<P>I don’t know, what do you guys think?   <BR>It might help keep things from getting out of hand.<BR>Also if you don’t think this is a good idea: Just Vote To Delete.||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||05-23-2000||02:49 PM||||If this was real-time chat, I might agree. Right now, what we don't police ourselves, Cliff cleans up. I like it that way. I know it's a little upsetting to have a conflict, especially when we went so long without a problem. We're a diverse group and rapidly growing. There's bound to be a few tensions and a situation that gets out of hand once in a while. But will will survive and become stronger because of it. It's hard to make rules to fix human nature.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick||05-23-2000||06:40 PM||||<BR>We don't need 1074 (at last count) moderators here.<P>What we do need is a little common sense and courtesy exhibited by <I>everyone</I> who makes use of this forum.||||reg||1
Z||000003||frontal lobe||05-23-2000||11:35 PM||||I have to agree with Batboy and Patrick.  I can understand the concept, but when you think about it, the actual number of problem threads has been very small.  There have been some pretty big blow-outs, but then everyone got back to helping each other with Fieros and being friends, or at least cordial.||||reg||1
